# Repos a reviewer of THIS repo may search and cite, materialized under
# .siblings/<owner>/<repo>. Declared rather than left to the fallback so
# the set is the one this repo actually depends on.
#
# One per line. The reviewer host must also carry a SOURCE_PATHS entry for
# each, or the sibling reports as `missing` and is never searched.
#
# This list must gain a row when README.md's fleet table does — the table is
# the authority for which agent repos exist, this file only makes them
# searchable. The dependency table beside it is the authority for the rest of
# the INTERNAL ones. `plow-hermes-agent` is one of those and IS listed: the
# fleet now runs its published base, so a review that cannot read it cannot see
# what the pinned digest actually contains. Its own upstream,
# `nousresearch/hermes-agent`, stays out — pinned by digest, never read as
# source, and materializing a third-party runtime on every review would cost
# more than the drift it could catch.

